@startuml admin_usecase
' DermaTrack — Admin use cases (screens/admin/* + services/admin_service).
' ONLY what is implemented. NOT implemented (shown as a note, not use cases):
' educational-content / FAQ / notification-template / support-ticket mgmt.
left to right direction
skinparam actorStyle awesome
actor "Admin" as A
actor "Super admin\n(review)" as SA

rectangle "Admin capabilities" {
  usecase "Log in / Sign out" as C1
  usecase "System monitoring overview\n(user/role counts, deactivated,\nactive break-glass)" as C2
  usecase "View / search users" as C3
  usecase "Change user role\n(patient/doctor/admin)" as C4
  usecase "Activate / deactivate account" as C5
  usecase "View audit log" as C6
  usecase "Open break-glass session\n(patient, reason, 15/30/60 min)" as C7
  usecase "View patient records under break-glass\n(read-only, time-limited)" as C8
  usecase "Revoke break-glass session" as C9
  usecase "Moderate chats\n(view all threads)" as C11
  usecase "Remove a message" as C12
  usecase "Restrict / unrestrict\nuser messaging" as C13
  usecase "Write audit entry" as C10
}

A --> C1
A --> C2
A --> C3
A --> C4
A --> C5
A --> C6
A --> C7
A --> C8
A --> C9
A --> C11
A --> C12
A --> C13

C4 .> C10 : <<include>>
C12 .> C10 : <<include>>
C13 .> C10 : <<include>>
C5 .> C10 : <<include>>
C7 .> C10 : <<include>>
C7 .> C8 : <<include>>
C9 .> C10 : <<include>>
C10 --> SA : reviewed by

note bottom of C8
  Break-glass grants read-only access to the patient's
  scans + patient_histories ROWS during an active session
  (RLS has_active_break_glass). Scan IMAGES are NOT exposed
  (no break-glass storage policy).
end note
note right of A
  NOT in code (excluded on purpose): educational-content,
  FAQ, notification-template, and support-ticket management.
end note
@enduml
